Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: defer interval-eight IN endpoint enable

Keep DMA request ownership while postponing EPENA to target minus three
microframes. Guard timer lifetime and preserve late request recovery.
Expose scheduling/CPU counters. This policy only applies to high-speed
buffer-DMA interval-eight IN endpoints. Runtime low-resolution timers
retain immediate enabling.

Prepared requests delayed beyond two milliseconds resynchronize on a
host NAK instead of reconstructing an ambiguous elapsed SOF count.

Hardware performance is not established by native source tests.
